# Stage 3: Component State Awareness Implementation Plan

This stage focuses on "Deep State Reporting". Instead of just sending a title, we will send full component metadata (priority, status, due dates) so the AI can reason about them (e.g., "Which of my tasks is most urgent?").

## Proposed Changes

### Frontend: Deep State Reporting

#### [NEW] [componentSchemas.ts](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/lib/componentSchemas.ts)
Define precise TypeScript interfaces for the "AI View" of each component.
- `TaskAIView`: title, priority, status, due_date, course_code.
- `AssignmentAIView`: title, course_code, user_status, due_at.
- `TimetableAIView`: module_code, time, venue, lesson_type.

#### [MODIFY] [DashboardPage](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/app/page.tsx)
- Upgrade the `useEffect` that reports `visibleItems` to use these deeper schemas.

#### [MODIFY] [TasksPage](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/app/tasks/page.tsx) & [AssignmentsPage](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/app/assignments/page.tsx)
- Integrate [useUIDispatch](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/lib/UIContextProvider.tsx#72-77) to report state when these pages are active.

